!! Vitals

* ''Branch'' `feature/lararium-node-5`, ahead of `origin` — `git rev-list --count origin/feature/lararium-node-5..HEAD` reads the unpushed commits; the operator pushes. Crew-held dirt in the tree: `mempalace` and `VSCode-TW5-Syntax` (submodule pointers), `tests/harness/instance.ts`, untracked `tests/e2e/nexus-offering-replication.test.ts`, `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/`, `.worktrees/`, `.claude/worktrees/`. Never commit, stash, or revert those.
* ''Landed in the last sign-off'' (CHANGELOG `[Unreleased]`, the SIGN-OFF BATCH lines): signed seal rolls (`seal-roll`); the herm's rung ladder (silent, waymark, temple) behind one closed door; any-face invites (`nexus-invite`), the `seat` arm refused as `seat-standing-owed`; `frameShape`/`verdictOf`; `scanAhu`; the charter seal-state readings; the boot fault's `fatal:` line; parallel-draft alerts; the bulb as the coal, named by the seed's published bytes; the quoteblock floor inside the deserializer, so every door fences; the gate reading its frame once; the clockless device edge; `KahuQuorumSeats`.
* ''E2E'' (the whole staged set): 28 of 29 files. The one red: the crew's untracked `tests/e2e/nexus-offering-replication.test.ts`.
* ''The witness fleet'' (`tools/witness-all.sh`, what CI runs) ends on a verdict table, one line per witness with its own exit code — count the reds there, never in the transcript. 31 read ok; `vessel-parity-witness` alone reads red (`makePersonaGroupIdentityRing` composes on node only — the browser side is owed). Each dist-reading witness refuses a stale build by name (exit 2) — rebuild the named package, run `node tools/stamp-build.mjs . --pkg <name>`, re-run; a comment edit in a package's `src/` stales its dist too.
* ''Typecheck'' (`tools/typecheck-witness.sh`): every package clean across 11 projects.
* ''Unit suites'': `lararium-tw5` 1732 passed, 1 red: `tests/carrier-edges.test.ts` reads 174 dangling edges against a ceiling of 172 — the +2 stand in the crew's research meme (`650a8e475`), theirs to settle; `lararium-mesh` 2427; `lararium-node` 1375; `lares-cli` 553; `lararium-keyhive` 146; `lararium-browser` 141; `lararium-memetic-frame` 354.
* ''HEADS-UP — the operator's live `~/.lares` vessel'': its stored device edges were signed over the clocked layout, and any rotated seal lineage it holds carries no signed rolls. Both fail verification on this build. Do NOT stand that vessel on this build; it needs the re-found or a re-mint.
* ''CI'' (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`): the last run read a pushed head behind the local tree — `gh run list --branch feature/lararium-node-5` names it. The next push is the witness for everything since.
* ''The tree is shared'': a parallel lane edits `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/wsl2/**` and `tools/wsl2/**` and re-stamps after editing — a witness run mid-edit reads its carriers as drifted for a minute. Re-run before believing a red there.
* ''Known test reds'' and their owners:
** `lararium-tw5` `tests/carrier-edges.test.ts` — the offering-antigen crew (above).
** `lararium-sensorium` `scripts/test_structure_router.py::test_ahu_block_nests_inner_sigils` reads one inner sigil where it asserts two — red on the desk and in CI.
** `tests/e2e/nexus-offering-replication.test.ts` — the Offering crew's.
** `lararium-tw5` `tests/syncer-back-parity.e2e.test.ts` (Chromium legs) and `tests/meme-routes.e2e.test.ts` — environmental when a browser or server socket is missing.
** `lararium-tw5` corpus suites can fail on `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/wsl2/*.mem` while that lane edits them — its owner's to settle.

