!! Open wounds, ranked

The sign-off accepted every lane and found no blocker; what it found stands here in the order to take it.

# ''The herm's `/oracle/*` and `/api/health` answer on the silent rung.'' An operator ruling: (a) closed-door refusals at once, then (b) peers prove first, or (c) an opt-in rung.
# ''`PresentationFinding` reaches no one.'' Surface it at the four presenter callers.
# ''A bag door lands a torn frame.'' LOAD and native ingest land a torn frame as one verbatim record; refuse it there instead, or rule that it lands.
# ''The keyring keys by lineage depth.'' Key it by `epochCid`.
# ''Hygiene'': collapse `presentedAdmitFromBoard` into `presentationFromBoardDoc`; spell `CLOSED_DOOR` once; a design call on `/cas` timing; whether the parallel-draft alert persists; `tools/herm-mesh-partition.mjs` reads the gone `pointer.version`.

''Carried, unranked''
* Road (iv): surface-for-review.
* Q6: loans keyed by CID.
* `packages/lararium-sensorium/requirements.txt` calls the tree-sitter versions one (Python binding 0.26, CLI 0.27; both ABI 15).
* The Sensorium red above.

''Pending operator rulings''
* ''R1/R2 — multi-carrier files.'' C2b, the `MemeStreamParser` deletion, waits on it.
* ''User-face standing'' (d): the gate withholds a user-face inviter until it rules (lean: the hosting hearth countersigns over the invite nonce — `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/the-invite`).
* ''Quieting the hearths-gate pass note.''

''Needs the operator''
* ''Grammar submissions'': whether the Nexus Kahu or the corpus-kahu receive them.
* ''The offering's `offer`/`witness` caps'' against the Lamplighter stack.
* ''Engine cadence, still open'' (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu` `#/contract`): who holds a cadence share; one daemon hosting two engine epochs; whether partial conformance lands before `kahuli engine` un-holds.
* ''Backstop seam (b), PHASE 5'' (`tests/meme-backstop.test.ts`): three child-edit shapes the test marks as the operator's call.
* ''Ruling-gated mesh modules'' (listed in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/index.ts`'s header): `recipe`, `readiness`, `reaction-graph` (canon memes pin their mesh `source-file`), `pronaos`, `offering-inspection` (own mesh-namespace memes). Each moves or stays only by ruling.
* ''The capture cell'' sits isolated for review in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-node/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/capture/`, `packages/lares-cli/src/commands/capture/`. Canon (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/capture-annotation-model`, the sensorium-machina S5 ruling) places capture in Python per stream with the TS @daemon coordinating only; the TS cell carries the live path. Rule: retire it to Python, or re-home it.
